From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:03:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl,
 VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library linked at the draw

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, KosmicKrisp advertises
VK_KHR_pipeline_library, VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library and its
graphicsPipelineLibrary feature, so DXVK's GPL path can run. Without the
flag nothing changes.

A pipeline library's state lacks the vertex input part or the fragment
output part, and KosmicKrisp's compile reads both. When the runtime
compiles shaders for such state (kk_gpl_partial_state), each shader keeps
only what a compile needs: its NIR serialized, the robustness state,
references to its set layouts, embedded samplers and push range, and the
fragment library's sample shading. A fast-linked pipeline binds these
shaders as they are.

Before its first draw, kk_gpl_resolve builds the whole pipeline's state
from the dynamic and rendering state: what the bound pipeline does not set
counts as dynamic. It keys that state by the shaders' hash plus the source
ids, and takes the shaders compiled for the key from the device's link
cache, compiling them as one pipeline on a miss. It then binds them the way
a whole pipeline's shaders are bound. A link-time-optimized link compiles
from the retained NIR as before.

This first step is correct but no faster: the draw still compiles. Making
the MSL of library shaders independent of the other libraries, so that a
link builds only the Metal pipeline, follows.
[kk-compile] link lines count links with MESA_KK_DEBUG=compile. Keys
tolerate the NULL parts of a library's state, library shaders are not
serialized, and meta operations save and restore the bound library
shaders.

Linear: PLA-424
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-kk-gpl-host.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
